Test Scenario 5 — Reconnection and Group Rejoin

In Window A (Number 1): open the browser's DevTools (F12) → Network tab → click the throttle dropdown → select "Offline". 
This simulates a network drop.

Watch Window A's header — after ~15 seconds, the dot turns red and "Reconnecting..." appears. The "Reconnecting" toast shows.

While Window A is offline, create a task from Window B. It appears on Window B and Window D but NOT on A (A is disconnected).

Set Window A back to Online in DevTools. Watch — SignalR reconnects, the onreconnected handler fires, invoke("JoinBoard", "engineering") runs, the server sends a fresh BoardState, and Window A's board re-populates including the task created while it was offline. 
The "Reconnected — refreshing board..." toast confirms success.


Testing Over Due Task Checker

Join a board, Create a task 
Set the due date to today or a past date and wait for 10s then, 
At the bottomm left corner the will be a small pop over saying there's an overdue task.
The pop over will continuosly appear until the task is marked complete

On the screenshot below, notice on the IN PROGRESS Column, next to the username SIBONELO, 
The is a time set for when the task is due, 
Then on the bottomm right corner the current time has exceeded the overdue time so the task is overdue
There is a pop up at the bottom right corner indicating that a task is overdue, and the tasks title is alse shown

